From 5559dfbec58d4304353d42feb7778c3dcd3edc28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Potin Lai <potin.lai@quantatw.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:03:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fru-device: fix redundant rescans on dbus property
 changes

The DBus event handler for CurrentHostState changes on the
xyz.openbmc_project.State.Host interface was previously triggering
unnecessary FRU rescans.

While the original logic did verify when the state changed to "Running",
it suffered from two issues:
1. It never updated the `powerIsOn` tracker to `false` when the host
   transitioned to other states (such as turning off).
2. The code that triggered the rescan was placed outside the property
   validation block. As a result, once `powerIsOn` became `true`, any
   subsequent DBus property change (such as RequestedHostTransition)
   would inadvertently trigger a full rescan.

This commit improves the handler by accurately updating the `powerIsOn`
state for both running and non-running states, and safely moving the
rescan invocation inside the state validation block. This ensures that
rescans are strictly limited to when the host successfully transitions
to the Running state, preventing unnecessary load on the daemon.

Signed-off-by: Potin Lai <potin.lai@quantatw.com>
Change-Id: I80eed110a5fef99df7207c9508ab2135e5554cf6

[1] Gerrit: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/95064
---
 src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp b/src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp
index 10d24135..56d4fcd4 100644
--- a/src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp
+++ b/src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp
@@ -1535,17 +1535,17 @@ int main()
             auto findState = values.find("CurrentHostState");
             if (findState != values.end())
             {
-                if (std::get<std::string>(findState->second) ==
-                    "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Host.HostState.Running")
+                bool isRunning =
+                    (std::get<std::string>(findState->second) ==
+                     "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Host.HostState.Running");
+
+                fruDetails.powerIsOn = isRunning;
+
+                if (isRunning)
                 {
-                    fruDetails.powerIsOn = true;
+                    rescanBusses(busMap, fruDetails, objServer);
                 }
             }
-
-            if (fruDetails.powerIsOn)
-            {
-                rescanBusses(busMap, fruDetails, objServer);
-            }
         };
 
     sdbusplus::match powerMatch = sdbusplus::match(
